# Real-scenario packing

Full contract: `docs/architecture/real_scenario.md`. Defect IDs `RS-1` ..
`RS-26` are tracked exceptions, not templates.

## Must

- Drive `DetectLuggage`, `ComputePlacement`, cargo-map commits, vacuum
  attach, and MoveIt collision from live perception plus allowed priors
  (container hull, empty-floor existence). Catalog suitcase WDH is
  spawn-only and must not fill those APIs.
- Keep Gazebo, `GetCurrentBox`, catalog AABB, and `eval_perfect_geometry`
  out of those APIs. Eval truth is a score numerator or dump only.
- Do not stamp GT or catalog size as `height_valid=true` or
  `HEIGHT_SOURCE_MEASURED_SUPPORT`.
- Do not treat `HEIGHT_SOURCE_CONFIGURED_SUPPORT` (`platform_z`) as measured
  FULL_3D geometry.
- Update cargo-map occupancy from live depth and/or a verified measured
  commit. An unverified planned slot is not occupancy.
- Do not copy `request.placed` from the same unverified plan used to fill
  `surface_2d` in order to hide commit–reality disagreement.
- Use `floor_prior` only as empty-floor existence when no accepted map
  exists, not as “the container is empty of cargo.”
- Do not authorize pick, MoveIt pickup AABB, or `ComputePlacement` without
  `height_source=MEASURED_SUPPORT`. TOP_ONLY is a detection, not grasp
  authority. Fail closed or wait/reobserve; do not invent height.
- Do not copy ROS1 `allow_gt_fallback`, `strict_perception=False`, gazebo
  inspect, or GT OBB carving into Humble.
- Do not branch production or production-API eval drivers on `sim_mode`,
  skip perception, or use a fake success path.
